an, who writes today that the company has lowered its sales forecasts for the device and cut orders for parts, citing an unnamed source. During the first 10 weeks of sales, the HomePod got just 10% of the smart speaker category’s sales, versus 73% for Amazon.com’s (AMZN) Echo devices, writes Gurman, and 14% for Alphabet’s (GOOGL) Google Home speaker. Apple shares today are up $2.06, or 1.2%, at $174.50. Reblog What to Read Next", "external_links": [], "published": "2018-04-12T17:23:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-04-13T16:42:31.009+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}